{%- comment -%}
  Gift wrap charge — the store-wide facts, and the script that keeps them true.

  Rendered ONCE per page from layout/theme.liquid. It has to be every page, not
  just the cart, because the cart can be changed from anywhere: the drawer's
  remove button and quantity stepper are on every template, and either of them
  can leave the wrapping charge standing for an item that is no longer there.
  Correcting that only on /cart would let a shopper who checks out from the
  drawer pay for wrapping nothing.

  WHY THE CHARGE IS A LINE ITEM
  Shopify builds cart totals out of line items and nothing else. A line item
  property or a cart attribute can carry information but not money, so charging
  for wrapping means keeping a line of `settings.gift_wrap_product` in the cart
  at a quantity equal to the number of wrapped units. That line is derived,
  never authored — gift-wrap.js recomputes it from the cart after every change.

  data-fee-current vs data-fee-needed is a staleness check that costs no
  request: what the cart charges for right now, against what the wrap selections
  call for. Equal on virtually every page view, and the script only reaches for
  the network when they disagree.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # RESOLVING THE CHARGE PRODUCT — kept identical in
  # snippets/gift-wrap-config.liquid and sections/main-cart-items.liquid.
  #
  # The picker wins, but a product whose handle is `gift-wrap` is picked up on
  # its own. That fallback exists because config/settings_data.json is part of
  # this repository: a value chosen in the theme editor is overwritten the next
  # time the theme is pushed from here, and the charge would quietly stop
  # applying. Naming the product Gift Wrap is enough to make it survive that.
  assign fee_product = settings.gift_wrap_product
  if fee_product == blank
    assign fee_product = all_products['gift-wrap']
  endif

  assign fee_product_id = ''
  assign fee_variant_id = ''

  if fee_product != blank
    # first_available_variant is nil when nothing is in stock, which would leave
    # the charge silently switched off. Falling back to the first variant keeps
    # it working — the product should have inventory tracking off anyway.
    assign fee_variant = fee_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    if fee_variant == blank
      assign fee_variant = fee_product.variants.first
    endif
    if fee_variant != blank
      assign fee_product_id = fee_product.id
      assign fee_variant_id = fee_variant.id
    endif
  endif

  assign fee_current = 0
  assign fee_needed = 0
  for item in cart.items
    if fee_product_id != blank and item.product.id == fee_product_id
      assign fee_current = fee_current | plus: item.quantity
    elsif item.properties['Gift wrap'] != blank
      assign fee_needed = fee_needed | plus: item.quantity
    endif
  endfor
-%}

<div
  id="GiftWrapConfig"
  hidden
  data-fee-variant="{{ fee_variant_id }}"
  data-fee-current="{{ fee_current }}"
  data-fee-needed="{{ fee_needed }}"
></div>

<script src="{{ 'gift-wrap.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
